WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.425
So what does the rule ask of you?

2
00:00:02.675 --> 00:00:05.075
Start with speed and readiness.

3
00:00:05.325 --> 00:00:11.850
Every vessel shall proceed at a safe speed adapted to the conditions of restricted visibility.

4
00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.650
That’s Rule six, with the fog pressed down hard on it.

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.650
A power-driven vessel shall have her engines ready for immediate maneuver.

6
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:23.675
No autopilot and a cup of coffee.

7
00:00:23.925 --> 00:00:26.000
A hand near the throttles.

8
00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:35.575
And every vessel applies Rules four through ten with the visibility in mind: the lookout, safe speed, risk of collision, and action to avoid it.

9
00:00:35.825 --> 00:00:38.450
So here’s what that looks like on your boat.

10
00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.300
Slow down.

11
00:00:40.550 --> 00:00:44.450
Put someone forward to listen, away from the engine noise.

12
00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:46.650
Sound your fog signals.

13
00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:50.150
Turn your navigation lights on, even at noon.

14
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.800
And if you have radar, plot every target, don’t just glance at it.

15
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.550
One more thing your passengers won’t like: quiet on deck.

16
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.200
In fog, your ears are a navigation instrument.
